## Section 6 — Certifications

The authorized official of the subrecipient organization must check each box to confirm compliance.

- [ ] The organization is **not presently debarred, suspended, proposed for debarment, or declared ineligible** for participation in federal assistance programs. This has been verified via **SAM.gov** (System for Award Management).

- [ ] The organization maintains **adequate financial management systems**, including the ability to segregate federal funds, track expenditures by award, and produce financial reports as required by 2 CFR 200.302.

- [ ] The organization will **comply with 2 CFR Part 200** (Uniform Administrative Requirements, Cost Principles, and Audit Requirements for Federal Awards) as applicable to the subaward.

- [ ] The organization will **comply with all applicable federal statutes, regulations**, executive orders, and award-specific terms and conditions that flow down from the prime award.

- [ ] The organization will **permit access to records** by {{ org_name }}, the federal awarding agency, the Comptroller General, and their authorized representatives, as required by 2 CFR 200.337.

- [ ] The organization will **submit financial and technical reports** in accordance with the schedule and format specified in the subaward agreement.

- [ ] If the organization's total federal expenditures equal or exceed **$1,000,000** in a fiscal year, it will have a **Single Audit** conducted in accordance with 2 CFR 200 Subpart F and will make the results available to {{ org_name }}.

- [ ] If the subaward involves **PHS- or NIH-funded research**, the organization has a current **Financial Conflict of Interest (FCOI) policy** that complies with 42 CFR Part 50, Subpart F; **OR** the organization agrees to comply with {{ org_name }}'s FCOI policy for the duration of the subaward.

- [ ] No covered individual of the organization **participates in a malign foreign talent recruitment program** (MFTRP) as defined in Section 10632 of the CHIPS and Science Act of 2022.

